# Task 159-003 Execution Plan

## Goal
Implement `deckent metrics summary <sprintId>` (and `--last`) CLI command that aggregates and renders agent + skill + provider compliance metrics from sprint artifacts.

## Files
- src/cli/commands/metrics.ts (new) — registerMetrics + helper functions (parsers, aggregators, table renderers)
- src/cli/index.ts — import + register
- tests/cli/commands/metrics.test.ts (new) — 5+ tests

## Data Sources
1. `.deckent/sprint-{id}-metrics.jsonl` — events: wave.start, result.collected, hb.stale, traces (durationMs)
2. `.tasks/archive/sprint-{id}-tasks/task-*.json` — task definitions (assignedAgent, assignedSkills, provider, model)
3. `.tasks/archive/sprint-{id}-tasks/task-*.result` — selfAssessment, filesChanged, tokenUsage
4. `.tasks/archive/sprint-{id}-tasks/task-*.result.fallback-attempt-N` — fallback events
5. Fall-back: if no archive dir, read live `.tasks/` for current/in-flight sprint

## Output Sections (markdown)
- Header: `Sprint <id> — Metrics Summary`
- Provider Distribution: provider, tasks, DONE, NO_GO, avg duration
- Model Distribution: model, tasks, routing (always "direct" until we have re-routing telemetry)
- Agent Compliance: agent, assigned, used, compliance%
- Skill Compliance: skill, assigned, used (proxy = filesChanged scope match)
- Fallback Events: list of `task-XXX: fromProvider → toProvider (reason)`
- Honesty/Coverage Drift: count of tasks with selfAssessment=DONE but tests not actually run/pass

## Approach
- Pure helper functions (parseMetricsJsonl, scanArchive, aggregateProviderStats, aggregateModelStats, aggregateAgentStats, aggregateSkillStats, scanFallbackEvents, computeHonestyDrift, renderMarkdownTable, renderSummary) → testable in isolation.
- `--last` resolves the most-recent sprint by reading sorted archive dirs or sprint metrics files (prefer archive presence; else fall back to .deckent/sprint-*-metrics.jsonl with highest sprint number).
- "Compliance" for agent: how many of the assigned-agent tasks reached DONE/GO_WITH_TECH_DEBT (i.e., the worker stayed in role). For "(generic)" we count tasks without assignedAgent.
- "Used" for skill: filesChanged contains at least one path that overlaps with task.scope.directories (proxy), OR result was DONE/GO_WITH_TECH_DEBT.
- Avg duration: derived from sprint metrics traces or task createdAt → result mtime difference.
- Graceful: if sprint has no archive AND no metrics file → print friendly "no data found" message and exit 0.

## Tests (target 7+)
1. `parseMetricsJsonl` — handles valid jsonl, ignores invalid lines
2. `aggregateProviderStats` — counts DONE/NO_GO and computes avg duration correctly
3. `aggregateModelStats` — collects unique models with counts
4. `aggregateAgentStats` — handles generic (missing assignedAgent) bucket
5. `aggregateSkillStats` — uses filesChanged proxy correctly
6. `scanFallbackEvents` — finds and reports fallback-attempt-N files
7. CLI flag parse — `summary <sprintId>` and `summary --last` resolve correctly
8. Missing sprint graceful message
9. Render full markdown contains every section header

## Verify
- `tsc --noEmit`
- `npx vitest run tests/cli/commands/metrics.test.ts`
- `npx vitest run` (full)
